# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Support for multi-process and multi-threaded acceleration for the latest version of Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"
msgstr "Suporta para sa multi-process at multi-threaded na akselerasyon para sa pinakabagong bersyon ng Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Support for multi-process and multi-threaded acceleration"
msgstr "Suporta para sa multi-process at multi-threaded na akselerasyon"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Support for multi-process and multi-threaded acceleration {#support-for-multi-process-and-multi-threaded-acceleration}"
msgstr "Suporta para sa multi-process at multi-threaded na akselerasyon {#support-for-multi-process-and-multi-threaded-acceleration}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This page documents the extent to which `qiskit-addon-sqd` supports multi-threaded and multi-process acceleration, and the assumptions that a high-performance-computing (HPC) developer can rely on when integrating this package into an accelerated workload.\n"
msgstr "Inilalarawan ng pahinang ito kung hanggang saan sinusuportahan ng `qiskit-addon-sqd` ang multi-threaded at multi-process na akselerasyon, at ang mga pagpapalagay na maaaring asahan ng isang high-performance-computing (HPC) developer kapag isinasama ang package na ito sa isang pinabilis na workload.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The single-threaded assumption {#the-single-threaded-assumption}"
msgstr "Ang pagpapalagay na single-threaded {#the-single-threaded-assumption}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unless otherwise specified, the APIs in this package are meant to be called from a single thread. High-level APIs exposed by this package are not guaranteed to be re-entrant, and end users should not invoke them from any thread other than the main thread.\n"
msgstr "Maliban kung iba ang tinukoy, ang mga API sa package na ito ay nilalayong tawagin mula sa iisang thread. Ang mga high-level na API na inilalantad ng package na ito ay hindi garantisadong re-entrant, at hindi dapat tawagin ng mga end user ang mga ito mula sa anumang thread maliban sa main thread.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collective multi-process execution {#collective-multi-process-execution}"
msgstr "Collective na multi-process na pagpapatupad {#collective-multi-process-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This package supports collective multi-process acceleration in the single-program, multiple-data (SPMD) style, in which the entire program is launched as multiple isolated processes that run with explicit global synchronization and communication between them (for example, `mpirun -n 128 python my_program.py`). Because the SPMD style composes cleanly with job schedulers and other parallel software and scales to large process counts, it is the recommended model for high-performance and large-scale workloads, and it is the subject of this page.\n"
msgstr "Sinusuportahan ng package na ito ang collective na multi-process na akselerasyon sa istilong single-program, multiple-data (SPMD), kung saan ang buong programa ay inilulunsad bilang maraming hiwalay na process na tumatakbo na may tahasang global na synchronization at komunikasyon sa pagitan nila (halimbawa, `mpirun -n 128 python my_program.py`). Dahil maayos na nakakasama ang istilong SPMD sa mga job scheduler at iba pang parallel na software at nakakapag-scale sa malaking bilang ng process, ito ang inirerekomendang modelo para sa mga high-performance at malakihang workload, at ito ang paksa ng pahinang ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Although this package is designed to accommodate different collective-execution backends, its current implementation targets MPI, the standard message-passing API for HPC systems. Regardless of implementation, this package assumes that a single thread controls each process. In the case of MPI, this corresponds to `MPI_THREAD_FUNNELED` or lower.\n"
msgstr "Bagaman idinisenyo ang package na ito para tumanggap ng iba't ibang collective-execution backend, ang kasalukuyang implementasyon nito ay nakatuon sa MPI, ang standard na message-passing API para sa mga HPC system. Anuman ang implementasyon, ipinapalagay ng package na ito na iisang thread ang kumokontrol sa bawat process. Sa kaso ng MPI, tumutugma ito sa `MPI_THREAD_FUNNELED` o mas mababa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a function supports collective execution, its documentation must say so. If the documentation does not mention collective execution, the function has no collective semantics and must be called from the control process alone.\n"
msgstr "Kung sinusuportahan ng isang function ang collective execution, dapat itong sabihin ng dokumentasyon nito. Kung hindi binabanggit ng dokumentasyon ang collective execution, walang collective semantics ang function at dapat itong tawagin mula sa control process lamang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The specific return-value and synchronization semantics of a collective function are documented with the function itself. In general, that documentation should make clear:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga partikular na semantics ng return value at synchronization ng isang collective function ay nakadokumento kasama ng function mismo. Sa pangkalahatan, dapat gawing malinaw ng dokumentasyong iyon ang:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Whether the function is meant to be called independently by each process on its own local data, or collectively by all processes.\n"
msgstr "Kung ang function ay nilalayong tawagin nang hiwalay ng bawat process sa sarili nitong lokal na data, o collective ng lahat ng process.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "How its arguments must agree across processes.\n"
msgstr "Kung paano dapat magkasundo ang mga argumento nito sa lahat ng process.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "How its return value is delivered—whether the result exists only on the control process, whether all processes receive the same value, or whether each process receives a handle to a local portion of a distributed data structure.\n"
msgstr "Kung paano inihahatid ang return value nito—kung ang resulta ay umiiral lamang sa control process, kung tumatanggap ang lahat ng process ng parehong halaga, o kung tumatanggap ang bawat process ng handle sa isang lokal na bahagi ng isang distributed na data structure.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Only one function currently supports being called collectively from all processes: [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\"). When it is invoked collectively, the eigensolver step is where all processes participate and contribute work, so an eigensolver implementation can use every process. The remaining parts of the configuration-recovery loop have no distributed implementation and run on the control process (rank 0) only.\n"
msgstr "Isang function lamang ang kasalukuyang sumusuporta sa pagtawag nang collective mula sa lahat ng process: [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\"). Kapag tinawag ito nang collective, ang hakbang ng eigensolver ang kung saan lumalahok at nag-aambag ng trabaho ang lahat ng process, kaya magagamit ng isang implementasyon ng eigensolver ang bawat process. Ang natitirang bahagi ng configuration-recovery loop ay walang distributed na implementasyon at tumatakbo lamang sa control process (rank 0).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every subspace of an iteration is passed to the eigensolver in a single call, so an implementation is free to divide the processes into groups and diagonalize several subspaces in parallel. How a solver uses the processes available to it is a property of that eigensolver.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat subspace ng isang iteration ay ipinapasa sa eigensolver sa iisang tawag, kaya malaya ang isang implementasyon na hatiin ang mga process sa mga grupo at i-diagonalize nang magkakasabay ang ilang subspace. Ang paraan ng paggamit ng isang solver sa mga process na magagamit nito ay katangian ng eigensolver na iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some existing eigensolver implementations require the calling program to run outside an MPI/SPMD environment, because they launch and manage their own parallel processes internally, for example by invoking `mpirun` on the user’s behalf. That mode is convenient for interactive and notebook-based work and remains supported; its requirements on the calling program are described in the API reference of the [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\") function.\n"
msgstr "Ang ilang umiiral na implementasyon ng eigensolver ay nangangailangang tumakbo ang tumatawag na programa sa labas ng isang MPI/SPMD na environment, dahil sila mismo ang naglulunsad at namamahala ng sarili nilang mga parallel na process sa loob, halimbawa sa pamamagitan ng pagtawag sa `mpirun` para sa user. Maginhawa ang mode na iyon para sa interactive at notebook-based na trabaho at nananatiling suportado; ang mga kinakailangan nito sa tumatawag na programa ay inilalarawan sa API reference ng function na [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Error handling in a multi-process context {#error-handling-in-a-multi-process-context}"
msgstr "Paghawak ng error sa multi-process na konteksto {#error-handling-in-a-multi-process-context}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A function that is called collectively from all processes must not raise an exception or abort only a single process, because that would leave the remaining processes deadlocked or in an inconsistent state. Instead, error handling follows fail-stop semantics for the execution context as a whole: upon an error, the implementation must be prepared to abort the entire execution context collectively (for example, by using `MPI_Abort`).\n"
msgstr "Ang isang function na tinatawag nang collective mula sa lahat ng process ay hindi dapat mag-raise ng exception o mag-abort ng iisang process lamang, dahil iiwan nitong deadlocked o nasa hindi pare-parehong estado ang natitirang mga process. Sa halip, sumusunod ang paghawak ng error sa fail-stop semantics para sa buong execution context: kapag may error, dapat handa ang implementasyon na i-abort nang collective ang buong execution context (halimbawa, sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng `MPI_Abort`).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The API cannot guarantee coordinated error reporting or collective delivery of exceptions across processes, because MPI implementations do not provide such guarantees. An implementation might additionally attempt to make an error visible to all participating processes—for example, by having each process raise an exception—but this can only be provided on a best-effort basis and must not be relied upon for correctness or recovery.\n"
msgstr "Hindi magagarantiya ng API ang koordinadong pag-uulat ng error o collective na paghahatid ng mga exception sa mga process, dahil hindi nagbibigay ng ganoong garantiya ang mga implementasyon ng MPI. Maaaring subukan din ng isang implementasyon na gawing nakikita ang isang error sa lahat ng kalahok na process—halimbawa, sa pamamagitan ng pagpapa-raise ng exception sa bawat process—ngunit best-effort lamang ito at hindi dapat asahan para sa kawastuhan o recovery.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These are properties that a collective implementation is permitted to have, not guarantees about any particular one. In this package, the only collective step is the eigensolver (see the preceding section); its default implementation is not distributed, so these considerations apply to a custom, collective eigensolver supplied by the user.\n"
msgstr "Ito ay mga katangiang pinapayagang taglayin ng isang collective na implementasyon, hindi mga garantiya tungkol sa alinmang partikular. Sa package na ito, ang tanging collective na hakbang ay ang eigensolver (tingnan ang naunang seksyon); hindi distributed ang default na implementasyon nito, kaya ang mga konsiderasyong ito ay nalalapat sa isang custom, collective na eigensolver na ibinibigay ng user.\n"
